    "title": "Luers grad Hammock back to NFL as Seattle's RB coach - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Glenn Marini ,\n5 hours ago\nSEATTLE, Wash. (WANE) – Bishop Luers High School graduate Thomas Hammock is headed back to the NFL after spending seven seasons at the head coach at Northern Illinois University, as the former Highlight Zone star will be the running backs coach of the Seattle Seahawks.\nHammock will reportedly be the highest-paid running backs coach in the NFL, and will also serve as a senior offensive assistant in Seattle.\nHammock went 35-47 with Northern Illinois – his alma mater – including a win over then-no 5. Notre Dame in 2024. He was inducted into the Indiana Football Hall of Fame last summer .\nPrior to his time at Northern Illinois, Hammock spent five seasons as the running backs coach with the Baltimore Ravens. Current Seahawks head coach Mike Macdonald was an assistant with the Ravens during Hammock’s time in Baltimore.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
